menu "Button box"

config BOX_BUTTON_GPIO
    int "Button GPIO"
    default 9 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C2 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32H2
    default 28 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5
    default 0
    help
        The GPIO the button is on, wired to ground (pressed = low; the internal
        pull-up holds it high). The default is the board's BOOT button, so a dev
        board works with no wiring: GPIO0 on the ESP32 and ESP32-S3, GPIO9 on the
        C2, C3, C6 and H2, GPIO28 on the C5.

config BOX_NAME
    string "Advertised name"
    default "Button Box"
    help
        What scanners (and the badge's active scan) show. At most 29 bytes.

endmenu
